cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use SeabornMasterPro in research, please cite it as below."
title: "SeabornMasterPro: research-grade statistical visualization on top of Seaborn"
type: software
version: 2.0.0
date-released: 2026-09-27
license: GPL-3.0-or-later
repository-code: "https://github.com/SatvikPraveen/SeabornMasterPro"
url: "https://github.com/SatvikPraveen/SeabornMasterPro"
authors:
  - family-names: Praveen
    given-names: Satvik
    email: satvikpraveen707@gmail.com
keywords:
  - seaborn
  - matplotlib
  - statistical visualization
  - reproducibility
  - effect sizes
  - bootstrap
  - colour vision deficiency
  - publication figures
abstract: >-
  SeabornMasterPro is a typed Python package and eleven-notebook curriculum for
  producing publication-quality statistical graphics with Seaborn. It adds bootstrap
  confidence intervals, effect sizes with multiplicity-corrected pairwise tests,
  colour-vision-deficiency palette validation, journal-specific figure geometry, and
  provenance embedded in exported figures, together with deterministic synthetic
  datasets described by data cards and verified by a SHA-256 manifest.
references:
  - type: article
    title: "seaborn: statistical data visualization"
    authors:
      - family-names: Waskom
        given-names: Michael L.
    journal: Journal of Open Source Software
    volume: 6
    issue: 60
    year: 2021
    doi: 10.21105/joss.03021
